<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jindeok of Silla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 654</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jindeok was queen of Silla from 647 to 654, the second woman to rule the kingdom. She came to the throne during the rebellion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidam">Bidam</a>, which was put down by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kim-yu-sin">Kim Yu-sin</a>. Guided by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muyeol-of-silla">Kim Chunchu</a>, she tied Silla closely to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>, adopting Tang court dress and Tang era names. She was the last ruler from Silla's highest 'hallowed bone' rank.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jindeok-of-silla.jpg" alt="Jindeok of Silla" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Asta · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Tomb_of_Queen_Jindeok.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
